{{Wireless adapter |brand=HP |model=BOISB-0410-00 |revision= |asin= |manuf_country=China |is_manuf=No |manuf=Z-Com |manuf_model= |manuf_rev= |availability= |fcc_date=01/25/2005 |fcc_id=B94BOISB0410 |ic_id=466F-BOISB410 |if=SPI (module) |if_bus_version= |if_connector_type= |form_factor=module |vendor_id= |device_id= |chip1_brand=Marvell |chip1_model=88W8385;88W8385-TGJ1, F627341.6, 0436 B0P ES, Taiwan; |chip2_brand=Marvell |chip2_model=88W8010;88W8010-NNB1, K296141.3, 0418 B4P; |accessible_UART=No |addl_chips= |id_string= |flags= |ant_conn=none |802dot11_protocols=bg |oui= |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} {{TagLine|Firenze Wireless Radio Module}}
"SPI Module V04" is silkscreened on the board in the FCC photos.
Per the FCC label, ''[[Z-Com]]'' appears to be the manufacturer.
This module appears to be used in the [[HP]] LaserJet 1022nw.
